From be0eb85812d16b8765d3d03ee17c64d79b3c5c3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:36:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/28] cellSpurs: CellSpursQueue as the SPU library lays it
 out; real push and pop

The title's own SPU library (Bullet's collision task in 3D Dot Game
Heroes, push at LS 0x2AE18, pop at 0x2B630) defines the line:
W0 pop / W1 push index at 0x00/0x04 (inverted while an SPU moves data),
element size 0x08, depth 0x0C, buffer 0x10, direction 0x1C, pop-waiter
rings at 0x20 (task ids) / 0x40 (workload ids), push-waiter rings at
0x30 / 0x50 (byte 0 count, FIFO; the woken head removes itself).

The initialiser wrote size and buffer at 0x10/0x18 and the push was a
logged no-op, so every command a title pushed was silently dropped and
cellSpursQueuePopBody was missing. Push (PPU2SPU) and pop (SPU2PPU) now
move the element and the index in one step under the lock-line lock and
wake the head waiter of the other side; a full/empty queue is polled.
Clear, Size and DetachLv2EventQueue follow the same layout.
